# Idempotent map reset (OCC-GRID-CONSUMER-COMPAT G1, I1).
#
# The legacy /cargo_map/reset service keeps its premise-less semantics
# (fresh operation id per call, no replay). This v2 interface binds a
# caller reset_id: retries with the same id and the same content replay
# (ALREADY_PROCESSED); the same id with different content is refused
# (OPERATION_ID_CONFLICT); a declared expected_epoch that is not the
# current epoch is refused (EPOCH_MISMATCH) instead of wiping a newer
# map. The reset linearization point rotates the epoch and moves the
# validity lifecycle to INVALID then BUILDING (two latched events).
string reset_id
string expected_epoch
string reason
---
string status          # OK|ALREADY_PROCESSED|OPERATION_ID_CONFLICT|EPOCH_MISMATCH|RESET_ID_REQUIRED|REJECTED
string epoch           # epoch AFTER the reset (UUID string, empty on refusal)
uint64 generation      # lifecycle generation AFTER the reset
uint64 resulting_map_revision
string content_digest
